+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+- A client may request its conversation summaries with `list_conversations`; `limit` is an integer from 1 through 200 and `before`, when present, is the complete `{updatedAt, sessionId}` cursor returned by an earlier page. Invalid values are refused with `INVALID_MESSAGE`. ([validated by: validates a list request and rejects each malformed limit or cursor by field name](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L94))
+- With `transport.history.enabled`, the server answers with one `conversation_list` containing the authenticated connection user's summaries newest first. It takes the user id only from the connection, forwards the requested window, renders both dates as ISO strings, carries no conversation content, and answers outside the per-session turn lock. ([validated by: answers from the authenticated user's store window before an in-flight turn ends](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L119))
+- History disclosure is independently opt-in. When it is disabled or the configured store cannot list, the server answers `UNSUPPORTED` rather than an empty `conversation_list`; a client opens a selected row through the existing authenticated resume query rather than an in-band switch. ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED, never an empty list, when history is off or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L172))
 
